+- Spool files live in the system temp directory (`TMPDIR`). Each is bounded by the output cap plus what the group writes before it is stopped: up to one poll interval (5 ms) until the overshoot is seen, then up to the kill grace (`KILL_GRACE`, 5 s) while the kill runs and the group exits. When the kill fails (`ProcessError::Kill`) the group may still be writing and no bound holds.
 - Attribute policing needs git 2.40 or later (`check-attr --source`), and `attr.tree` needs 2.42; an older git fails closed or ignores the setting (then in-tree attributes can only make numstat print `-`, which counts as maximum size).
 
